              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "декрет (dekrét) — \"maternity leave; a decree\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "После рождения сына она год была в декрете. Pósle rozhdéniya sýna oná god bylá v dekréte. After her son was born she was on maternity leave for a year."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Masculine. Colloquial for декретный отпуск. Its older sense is a decree."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "декрет (dekrét) was borrowed from Latin decretum 'a decree' (EtymDB), from dēcernere 'to decide' (Lewis & Short)."
            }
          ]
        },
